Objective: This 21 day email course is designed for the student to gain
a clear understanding of the credit repair process so that they can
approach the client file and create an action plan with certainty. The
content of this course is also designed to help the student effectively
communicate credit information so that as a business owner they can feel
comfortable and confident when speaking about the subject of credit to
leads, clients, and the general public.

Bonus Lesson #4:
Consumer Reporting Agencies

Bruce, When it comes to checking consumer reports and disputing
negative accounts, we're all familiar with the BIG 3: TransUnion,
Experian, & Equifax. But, did you know that there are more than 400
consumer reporting agencies in the United States? The information
contained in many of the reports these agencies provide to other
companies could many times be the very reason you or your clients are
being denied for credit as well as the key to successfully removing
negative information. 

As we move into the last phase of this course, dispute flows, I
encourage you to take a look at the list of consumer reporting companies
I've listed below. Aside from the Big 3, these are a few of the
companies that I frequently request reports from for my clients,
depending on the information I'm seeking. Many of these companies report
information and accounts that you will not find on a bureau report. It
is also important to note that some of these companies are not only
reporting agencies, but they also act as data furnishers. For example,
LexisNexis is many times the furnisher of public records information to
the bureaus. If you're having a hard time with a bankruptcy, LexisNexis
might be one of the agencies that you would want to contact to request a
consumer report and possibly dispute with before verifying an account
with either TransUnion, Equifax or Experian. If your client has an
eviction or a repossession, you just might want to contact one of the
agencies below to tackle that account first. 

I suggest that you get very familiar with the companies listed below as
well as others out there to find out what type of information they
collect and report. FYI...once you have the report, you request
verification from these agencies and follow the dispute process the same
as you would a credit bureau.  

Innovis 
(aka*4th Bureau)

Provides ID verification data to assist with fraud detection and
prevention. 

Free report: 
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. 

Freeze your report: 
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it. 

Website 
Innovis.com  
Request security freeze

Phone 
800-540-2505 

Address 
Innovis Consumer Assistance 
P.O. Box 1689 
Pittsburgh, PA 15230-1689 

LexisNexis Risk Solutions 

Collects information from public records and multiple proprietary data
sources. This includes items such as real estate transaction and
ownership data, lien, judgment, and bankruptcy records, professional
license information, and historical addresses on file. 

Free report: 
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. 

Freeze your report: 
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it. 

Website 
personalreports.lexisnexis.com

Request report form

and Instructions

Request security freeze

Phone 
866-897-8126 

Address 
LexisNexis Consumer Center 
Attn: Full File Disclosure 
P.O. Box 105108 
Atlanta, GA 30348-5108 

**ChexSystems**

Provides account verification services primarily for financial
institutions. Collects and reports data on checking account
applications, openings, and closures, including reasons for account
closure. When you apply for a new checking account many banks and credit
unions will refer to this database to help inform whether to approve
your new account. 

ChexSystems is affiliated with Fidelity National Information Services,
Inc. (FNIS)

**Free report and score:**
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. A free score will be provided upon request too.

**Freeze your report:**
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it.

**Website**
chexsystems.com  
Request report form

Request score form

Security freeze information

Security freeze form

****

**Phone** 
800-428-9623 or 
800-513-7125 

****

**Address**
ChexSystems, Inc.
Attn: Consumer Relations 
7805 Hudson Road, Suite 100 
Woodbury, MN 55125 

Clarity Services 

Collects and provides information on payday loans, installment loans,
auto loans (and leasing), check cashing services, rent-to- own
transactions, telecommunication account openings, and financial services
with an emphasis on the lower income and subprime consumer market
segments. 

*Clarity Services is owned by Experian. 

Free report and score: 
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. The company will also provide a credit risk score if you request it 

Freeze your report: 
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it. 

Website 
ClarityServices.com  
Request score

Request security freeze

Phone 
866-390-3118 
(Option 1 for security freeze; Option 4 for report request). 

Address 
Clarity Services, Inc. 
P.O. Box 5717 
Clearwater, FL 33758 

CoreLogic Credco 

Collects and reports personal data such as property ownership and home
loan obligation records; property legal filings and tax payment status;
rental applications and collection accounts; consumer bankruptcies,
liens, judgments, and child support obligations. 

Free report: 
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. 

Freeze your report: 
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it. 

Website 
CoreLogic.com/Credco

Request security freeze 

Phone 
877-532-8778 

Address 
CoreLogic Credco, LLC 
P.O. Box 509124 
San Diego, CA 92150 

SageStream 

This reporting company collects information from, and provides
supplementary consumer reports to, auto lenders, credit card issuers,
retailers, utilities and mobile phone service providers among other
service providers. 

SageStream is a subsidiary of ID Analytics. ID Analytics is a Symantec
Company. 

Free report: 
The company will provide one free report every 12 months if you request
it. 

Freeze your report: 
The company will freeze your consumer report if you request it. 

Website 
SageStream  
Request report  
Request security freeze 

Phone 
888-395-0277 

Address 
SageStream, LLC 
Consumer Office 
P.O. Box 503793 
San Diego, CA 92150 

